/root/autodl-tmp/symbolic_dynamics/docs/prior_work/legacy/5-riemann_henon/paper/manuscript.tex:59:Given this, our motivation is not to claim that RMT ``fails.'' Rather, we ask a constructive and complementary question: \emph{can a single, low-dimensional deterministic dynamical system generate, within one model and without a manual unfolding step, both the global mean density and the local repulsion of the zeros?} A positive numerical answer would not contradict RMT; it would offer a concrete dynamical object whose spectrum exhibits both scales simultaneously, in the spirit of the Hilbert--P\'olya program.
